Bash(gh pr create --label sandcastle --title "refactor(ocale): migrate game-passes wire code to by-domain layout" --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## Summary

Migrates the wire-level code for the `game-passes` Resource from the
peer Resource folder `src/resources/game-passes/` into a per-shape
sub-tree under `src/domains/game-passes/game-passes/`, per the
by-Domain layout established in
[ADR-022](docs/adr/022-by-domain-folder-layout-for-ocale.md).

After this PR, `src/resources/game-passes/` is a thin facade with only
`client.ts` and `index.ts`. `client.ts` imports builders, parsers,
operation-limit constants, and parsed-shape types from the new domain
sub-tree; `index.ts` re-exports the public types from the same
location. Wire requests, parsed shapes, and rate-limit operation keys
(`game-passes.get`, `game-passes.create`) are preserved end-to-end.

This is the second concrete migration under ADR-022 (after #300, which
absorbed `experience-icon` and `experience-thumbnails` into
`UniversesClient`). The conformance test (`parseGamePassResponse`
round-trips against the vendored OpenAPI fixtures) and the integration
test (`GamePassesClient` end-to-end) continue to drive the same public
surface; only their import paths into the package internals changed.

## Why

`game-passes` is one of the four peer Resource folders (alongside
`places`, `developer-products`, `universes`) that ADR-022 calls out
for the big-bang migration into the by-Domain layout, so future
endpoints sharing a Domain can co-locate their wire code and parsers
without per-Resource duplication. This PR is one slice of that
migration.

Closes #303.

